	(text "MCU\nESP32-S3 module, USB-C (programming + serial), boot/reset. All outputs default low = everything off."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 20.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5fd573a3-9889-4dbb-ae38-96efe9267d10")
	)
	(text_box "TO DESIGN\n- ESP32-S3 module on +3V3. USB-C on native USB (GPIO19/20): flashing + serial console, ESD protection, CC pull-downs 5.1k.\n- Reset RC on EN, BOOT and RESET buttons. No USB-UART bridge needed.\n- Watchdog: ESP32-S3 RTC watchdog (in silicon, independent of the CPU) resets the chip on a hang -> GPIOs float -> pull-downs switch all outputs off. External WDT left out: it would reset-loop during flashing and boot.\n- GPIO budget: 13 inputs + 11 outputs. Avoid strapping pins (0, 3, 45, 46) and the octal PSRAM pins (35-37 on R8 variants).\n  Output pins must not glitch high at boot. If the pins get tight: move the status inputs to an I2C expander (TCA9535).\n- Spare pins on a header (I2C, UART) for later extensions.\n- Wi-Fi: keep the antenna end of the module clear of copper and the metal housing (or use the -1U variant with external antenna).\n\nCOMPONENT PROPOSAL\n- Espressif ESP32-S3-WROOM-1-N16R8 (16 MB flash, 8 MB PSRAM - room for web UI and data logging).\n  Metal chamber housing: consider ESP32-S3-WROOM-1U-N16R8 + external antenna.\n- USB-C receptacle 16-pin (e.g. GCT USB4105-GF-A), ESD: ST USBLC6-2SC6.\n- Option: external watchdog (TI TPS3828) if the internal one proves insufficient.\n- 2x 6x6 mm tactile switch (BOOT, RESET)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 254 20.32 0)
		(size 152.4 48)
